From b465ee5415a41e0e54f62a637b9fe006d897ab90 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stephano Cetola <stephano@cetola.net>
Date: Wed, 8 Jul 2026 17:30:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 02/14] defaultenv: mnt-reform2-rk3588: add bootsource fallback
 boot script

barebox's extlinux scanner has no scan_disk handler and cannot scan an
MBR disk cdev directly. It only works when given a filesystem partition
cdev. bootsource_of_cdev_find() returns the disk cdev (e.g. mmc1) and
the extlinux provider finds zero entries, leaving auto-boot stuck.

Add /env/boot/bootsource to the mnt-reform2-rk3588 default environment.
This script is the fallback for the "bootsource" boot target. The DTS
chosen node maps barebox,bootsource-mmc0/1 to &sdhci/&sdmmc, enabling
bootsource_of_alias_xlate() to translate the BROM hardware instance to
the correct barebox device number ($bootsource_instance). The script
then boots mmc${bootsource_instance}.0 directly, bypassing the extlinux
scan_disk limitation.

Use [ ] || exit 1 instead of if/then to avoid the barebox hush
false-condition bug: run_list_real returns 0 when an if-condition is
false, causing bootscript_boot to report success even though nothing
was booted.
---
 .../boot/bootsource                           | 20 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 arch/arm/boards/mnt-reform2-rk3588/defaultenv-mnt-reform2-rk3588/boot/bootsource

diff --git a/arch/arm/boards/mnt-reform2-rk3588/defaultenv-mnt-reform2-rk3588/boot/bootsource b/arch/arm/boards/mnt-reform2-rk3588/defaultenv-mnt-reform2-rk3588/boot/bootsource
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..c01862b47a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/arch/arm/boards/mnt-reform2-rk3588/defaultenv-mnt-reform2-rk3588/boot/bootsource
@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@
+#!/bin/sh
+# Boot from the first partition of the bootsource MMC device.
+#
+# barebox's extlinux scanner has no scan_disk handler, so it cannot scan an
+# MBR disk cdev directly — it only works when given a filesystem partition
+# cdev.  bootsource_of_cdev_find() returns the disk cdev (e.g. mmc1), and
+# the extlinux provider returns zero entries, leaving auto-boot stuck.
+#
+# This script is the /env/boot/bootsource fallback: barebox tries it when
+# no bootentry provider finds entries for the "bootsource" boot target.
+# $bootsource_instance is resolved via barebox,bootsource-mmc0/1 phandles in
+# the DTS chosen node.
+#
+# On RCM5, barebox is loaded by the Rockchip miniloader + TF-A and enters at
+# EL2. rk3588_barebox_entry() only captures iRAM (0xff000000) when current_el
+# == 3, so the EL2 path leaves scratch uninitialized and $bootsource = "unknown".
+# Try the detected device first if bootsource worked, then fall back to
+# mmc1.0 (SD) and mmc0.0 (eMMC) unconditionally.
+[ "$bootsource" = "mmc" ] && boot mmc${bootsource_instance}.0
+boot mmc1.0 || boot mmc0.0
